{
  "dom_id": "step-q225123",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(5,0.63)$ given below, compute $P(2<X\\le 5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0069\\,$ | $\\,0.0660\\,$ | $\\,0.2670\\,$ | $\\,0.6093\\,$ | $\\,0.9008\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |\n\n$P(2<X\\le 5)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\})+P(X\\in \\{3,4,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)+P(2<X\\le 5) \\\\  & =F(2)+P(2<X\\le 5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X\\le 5) & =F(5)-F(2) \\\\  & =1.0000-0.2670 \\\\  & =0.7330.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
